# Backend Go Rules

Apply to modules listed in `go.work`.

- Write idiomatic Go with explicit error handling; propagate `context.Context`.
- Follow existing handler → service → repository separation where present.
- Do not use `panic` for normal request failures.
- Apply tenant predicates on tenant-owned data paths.
- Preserve stable HTTP semantics and validate inputs at boundaries.
- Use structured logging conventions from `packages/shared-go/logger` when adding logs.
- Add or update tests near changed behavior (`*_test.go` alongside changed packages).
- Avoid new global mutable state unless the architecture already requires it.
- Do not change backend business logic or API contracts unless the task explicitly authorizes it.
- Prefer `make health-check`, targeted `go test`, and service-scoped checks over full-stack startup for isolated tasks.
